  "claim": "The 1990s British romantic comedy that Charlotte Ninon Coleman played Scarlett in featured the song \"Love Is All Around\".",
  "evidencia": "Page: Reg Presley. Sentence: He wrote the song \"Love Is All Around\", which was featured in the films \"Four Weddings and a Funeral\" and \"Love Actually\".\nPage: Four Weddings and a Funeral. Sentence: Four Weddings and a Funeral is a 1994 British romantic comedy film directed by Mike Newell.\nPage: Charlotte Coleman. Sentence: Charlotte Ninon Coleman (3 April 1968 – 14 November 2001) was an English actress best known for playing Scarlett in the film \"Four Weddings and a Funeral\", Jess in the television drama \"Oranges Are Not the Only Fruit\", and her childhood roles of Sue in \"Worzel Gummidge\" and the character Marmalade Atkins.",
